{
  "info": {
    "name": "AnimeTube API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Every AnimeTube endpoint. Each request says who can call it in its description.\n\nHow to use:\n1. Start the server (npm run dev) and check the baseUrl variable (default http://localhost:8000/api/v1).\n2. Register, then Login. Postman keeps the accessToken and refreshToken cookies by itself.\n3. Admin requests need a user whose role is \"admin\". New users are \"user\", so change the role in the database by hand.\n4. Create requests save the new _id into collection variables (genreId, studioId, animeId, seasonId, episodeId, planId, reviewId), so the later requests work without copying ids.\n5. File fields (poster, banner, logo, video, thumbnail, profilePicture) are empty: pick a file before sending."
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000/api/v1"
    },
    {
      "key": "genreId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "studioId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "animeId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "seasonId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "episodeId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "planId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "reviewId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
